# build-kk-integration-cache-cu132.env -- karmic-kraken INTEGRATION (beta
# channel) assembly on the CUDA 13.2 / torch 2.13 aarch64 line, for
# build-spark-cache-cu132.sh. THE single serving profile: one image, kept at
# the most up-to-date LIL line, shared by every model it carries launchers
# for (GLM-5.3-Flash CSF first). The previously built image
# (karmic-kraken-integration-cache-cu132: vLLM f1c2508f + standalone b12x
# 52640cb1, Z1F) stays on the nodes as the fallback; this profile writes a
# NEW tag and never overwrites it.
#
# LIL CHANNELS (2026-10-08):
#   canonical  vLLM dev/karmic-kraken, image karmic-kraken-<date>: Luke's main
#              line; reviewed work lands here.
#   beta       vLLM integration/karmic-kraken-beta, image
#              karmic-kraken-beta-<date>: canonical + work still in review;
#              gets fixes first. THIS profile.
# On 2026-10-08 LIL rebuilt the beta on canonical (merge-base f88c893f) and
# both moved to FlashInfer 0.7.1 with B12X inside (the b12x repository is
# archived). For GLM-5.3-Flash the beta tip is AHEAD of canonical: it carries
# #1016 (CSF expert weights load straight into each layer's packed buffers;
# the old path reserved up to 92.5 GiB of GPU memory for 50 GiB of weights,
# and that is where LIL's "loading 214 -> 144 s" comes from). Canonical's
# only extra commits are a removed log line (636afde9), dense-NVFP4 hybrid A4
# (fa225346; Flash's dense layers are MXFP8) and a Qwen PLE load change.
# csrc/, cmake/, CMakeLists.txt, requirements/, setup.py and the three
# SparkCache patch targets are identical between the two tips.
#
#   component     LIL beta 20261008      here                   note
#   vllm          19f2c20e               19f2c20e (same)        integration/karmic-kraken-beta tip
#   flashinfer    LIL 0.7.1 b4c35e6e     b4c35e6e (same)        B12X inside; built here for 12.1f
#   b12x          inside FlashInfer      inside FlashInfer      B12X_SOURCE=flashinfer
#   lmcache       3171cdb5               3171cdb5 (same)
#   instanttensor 747390dc               747390dc (same)
#   nccl          2.31.2 cu134           2.30.4 cu132           kept (cu132 system-base)
#   torch         2.14 NGC               2.13.0+cu132           kept; vLLM still pins torch==2.13.0
#   cutlass-dsl   4.7.1                  4.7.1                  FlashInfer [b12x] extra pins ==4.7.1
#
# WHAT CHANGES FOR SERVING vs the f1c2508f fallback (the launcher
# glm-53-flash-csf_pair-serve.sh probes the image and adapts):
#   * NVFP4-CSF has no dedicated loader any more: --quantization
#     modelopt_mixed, with the CSF expert scales declared by ModelOpt recipes
#     (weight_scale_encoding: csf) in config.json. HF-layout checkpoints
#     (dec48abd) carry them; this image does not serve the container layout.
#   * --load-format b12x is built into vLLM (native B12xModelLoader, no
#     VLLM_PLUGINS entry; FlashInfer ships no b12x_loader plugin) and reads
#     CSF experts (vLLM 9cbd0066: CSF hooks accept the loader's file-backed
#     meta tensors). It loads into ordinary PyTorch CUDA allocations.
#   * Hybrid A4 prefill is semantic: B12X_W4A16_A4_PREFILL=1 runs EVERY
#     prefill row with NVFP4 activations (decode, verify, graph replay and
#     draft stay A16); B12X_W4A16_A4_PREFILL_MIN_TOKENS is removed.
#
# BUILD COST: build-base and base keep the f1c2508f toolchain (CUDA 13.2,
# torch 2.13, DSL 4.7.1) but carry this profile's tag, so they rebuild once
# unless SYSTEM_BASE_IMAGE / BUILD_BASE_IMAGE_TAG are pointed at the fallback
# image's bases. The FlashInfer stage is a FULL rebuild (new source, jit-cache
# provider for 12.1f) -- the longest stage and the one step never built on
# cu132/sm_121 before. vLLM's csrc/, cmake/, CMakeLists.txt are byte-identical
# to f1c2508f's era pins, so its compile is mostly ccache hits.

# Dated tag: specific about what it holds, and distinct from the fallback.
IMAGE_REPO=local/vllm
IMAGE_TAG=karmic-kraken-intcache1008-cu132
PROFILE_NAME=kk-intcache1008-cu132

# --- wrapper
LOGGING=1
# PIN_PREFLIGHT=1 also runs the CuTe DSL pre-flight: FlashInfer's [b12x]
# extra and the quack release must agree with CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION.
PIN_PREFLIGHT=1
MAX_JOBS=20
VLLM_MAX_JOBS=20
NVCC_THREADS=1
VLLM_NVCC_THREADS=1
PIN_SOURCE_COMMITS=1

# --- serving shape guard (both launchers exist at 19f2c20e)
VLLM_REQUIRED_LAUNCHERS=serve-glm53-flash-nvfp4.sh serve-ds4-flash-spark.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sources
# vLLM: integration/karmic-kraken-beta @ 19f2c20e (2026-10-08 15:19 +0200,
# merge of PR #1016 fix/csf-direct-packed-load), branch tip. Contains:
#   311c14b4 / 8c96e602  take B12X from FlashInfer 0.7.1; wheel requires it
#   a13af3fb             semantic hybrid A4 prefill + CSF scale prefetch
#   d0f0cad9             native --load-format b12x
#   9cbd0066             NVFP4-CSF hooks for B12X loader weight transfers
#   2e1293c4 (#1016)     CSF experts load straight into packed layer weights
#   28d74158 / f296393a  GLM-5.3 draft LM head (SM12x gate lifted)
#   + GLM-5.3 744B / DCP work in review (not on Flash's TP2/DCP1 path).
# Build-relevant delta vs f1c2508f: csrc/, cmake/, CMakeLists.txt, rust/,
# scripts/seccomp/ identical; requirements/cuda.txt (flashinfer-python==0.7.1,
# no standalone b12x) and setup.py changed. DeepGEMM still vendored at
# ad1f1726. torch==2.13.0 unchanged.
VLLM_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/vllm.git
VLLM_PIN=19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354

# B12X: no standalone source. FlashInfer 0.7.1 installs it as
# flashinfer/experimental/b12x plus a top-level `b12x` alias; the wrapper
# replaces the b12x stage with a check of that alias and labels the image's
# b12x commit with FLASHINFER_COMMIT. B12X_PIN must stay unset. The vendored
# copy carries b12x #483 (DSA indexer live-length merge), #485 (opt-in
# B12X_W4A16_SMALL_M_OCCUPANCY), #487 (CSF W4A16 small-M decode), the
# semantic A4 prefill (B12X_W4A16_A4_PREFILL) and b12x.loader (the io_uring
# checkpoint reader behind --load-format b12x).
B12X_SOURCE=flashinfer

# DeepGEMM: the vendored pin is still ad1f1726
# (cmake/external_projects/deepgemm.cmake).
DEEPGEMM_REPO=https://github.com/vllm-project/DeepGEMM.git
DEEPGEMM_REF=ad1f1726aa540a76c1d26d6a120effb8de21eaa4
DEEPGEMM_COMMIT=ad1f1726aa540a76c1d26d6a120effb8de21eaa4

# InstantTensor: 747390dc (LIL main; delta vs 95d4729b is arm64 CI only).
# --load-format instanttensor stays available as the A/B to b12x.
INSTANTTENSOR_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/InstantTensor.git
INSTANTTENSOR_REF=747390dc2bd1e0a18b0c7b13a09a38594edf342f
INSTANTTENSOR_COMMIT=747390dc2bd1e0a18b0c7b13a09a38594edf342f

# LMCache: integration/local-inference-lab @ 3171cdb5 (branch tip
# 2026-10-08; delta vs 820af25f is ci/lil_wheels/ only).
# LMCACHE_BUILD_VERSION = 0.5.3.dev<N>+lil.<sha8>, N from
# `git describe --tags --long --match 'v[0-9]*'` (v0.5.2-cu129-429).
# The beta reworked restore admission (kv_cache_manager -106 lines vs
# 64b96f45); LMCache's ef929e16 gates its restore-admission half on the vLLM
# API, so PREFIX_CACHE=lmcache needs its own test on this image.
LMCACHE_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/LMCache.git
LMCACHE_REF=3171cdb537de7af7d66d8e6ec7bf26bdcf3ba3bd
LMCACHE_COMMIT=3171cdb537de7af7d66d8e6ec7bf26bdcf3ba3bd
LMCACHE_BUILD_VERSION=0.5.3.dev429+lil.3171cdb5
PATCH_LMCACHE_INTEGRATION=on

# SparkCache: 801f7f9a (main HEAD 2026-10-08). vLLM patches regenerated
# against 19f2c20e: changed lines identical to the f1c2508f files, offsets
# only; zero offset/fuzz on 19f2c20e. Both hand fixes in 02 re-checked and
# still needed: allocate_slots keeps import_reserve, and
# can_admit_external_boundary_request still precedes the lease attach.
#   01-vmm-exemption       REQUIRED (expandable_segments guard).
#   02-shared-prefix-lease optional; NOT runtime-tested.
# GLM + SparkCache (aligned) still needs REPLAYSSM=0.
SPARKCACHE_REPO=https://github.com/FujitsuPolycom/sparkcache
SPARKCACHE_COMMIT=801f7f9a4bd83de8fddc35bda721089acf16584a
SPARKCACHE_VLLM_PATCHES=sparkcache-vllm-19f2c20e-01-vmm-exemption.patch,sparkcache-vllm-19f2c20e-02-shared-prefix-lease.patch
PATCH_SPARKCACHE=on

# fastokens: unchanged (0.3.2, PyPI latest). VLLM_USE_FASTOKENS and
# _MIN_FASTOKENS_VERSION=0.2.0 unchanged at 19f2c20e.
FASTOKENS_VERSION=0.3.2
FASTOKENS_SHA256=cbb29fae028d39a2020d01dfe587e1774a516b6d28641b70e83a285d460bdfb8
PATCH_FASTOKENS=on

# exllamav3: unchanged (EXL3 path, unrelated to GLM/KK).
EXLLAMAV3_COMMIT=704aefd743b390af4bd0fb429d1906f9b964c7d8

# ------------------------------------------------------------- toolchain
TORCH_VERSION=2.13.0+cu132
TORCHVISION_VERSION=0.28.0+cu132
TORCH_BUNDLED_NCCL_VERSION=2.29.7
NCCL_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/nccl-canonical.git
NCCL_REF=canonical/cu132-nccl2304-amd-noxml
NCCL_COMMIT=dfab7c1ace32da250ba97757879429c341b7bcf9
# FlashInfer: LIL 0.7.1 @ b4c35e6e -- head of integration/karmic-kraken-beta
# (the beta channel's FlashInfer) and of community/karmic-kraken-cu134-sm120
# on 2026-10-08 (LIL main 2f5210dd + wheel CI). Replaces voipmonitor
# 1ac69427 (0.6.18): this vLLM requires flashinfer-python==0.7.1. LIL builds
# it for CUDA 13.4 / torch 2.14 (12.0f); here it is built from source on
# cu132 / torch 2.13 for 12.1f (PATCH_GPU_ARCH) the way LIL's ci/lil_wheels
# does: python wheel, then the jit-cache provider
# (FLASHINFER_JIT_CACHE_PROVIDER_ARCH) and shim
# (FLASHINFER_JIT_CACHE_PROVIDER_ARCHS), BUILD_NVEP=0. The provider wheel is
# flashinfer-jit-cache-sm121f. REF = COMMIT (sha) so the branch cannot move
# under the build.
FLASHINFER_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/flashinfer.git
FLASHINFER_REF=b4c35e6ec1d712f6b832679c08ce5719fae57cd6
FLASHINFER_COMMIT=b4c35e6ec1d712f6b832679c08ce5719fae57cd6
FLASHINFER_BUILD_CUBIN=0
# FlashInfer 0.7.1 requirements.txt runtime dependencies at LIL's
# linux-arm64 lock versions (aarch64 wheels verified on PyPI 2026-10-08).
# Installed --no-deps in the FlashInfer stage before its import check, so no
# extra can pull an nvidia-nccl or cuda-bindings wheel; repeated in
# VLLM_RUNTIME_EXTRA_PACKAGES for the final stage. nccl4py MUST be >= 0.4.1:
# 0.3.1 still ships its own nccl/ep and collides with nccl-extensions.
FLASHINFER_RUNTIME_PACKAGES=nccl4py==0.4.1 nccl-extensions==0.1.0 cuda-core==1.0.1 cuda-pathfinder==1.6.0 cuda-tile==1.4.0 nvidia-cudnn-frontend==1.30.0
CUTLASS_REF=e6233cbac5d7c7a865c19c91cd684ceece19513c
CUTLASS_COMMIT=e6233cbac5d7c7a865c19c91cd684ceece19513c
# 4.7.1: FlashInfer's b12x extra pins ==4.7.1 (base, libs-base, libs-core,
# libs-cu12, libs-cu13); vLLM 19f2c20e's runtime.lock and
# requirements/cuda.txt say 4.7.1. PyPI 4.8.0 exists -- do not take it.
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.7.1
TILELANG_VERSION=0.1.12
TOKENSPEED_MLA_VERSION=0.1.8
TVM_FFI_VERSION=0.1.11
QUACK_KERNELS_SPEC=quack-kernels==0.6.5
# Pinned (was >=0.3.3): 0.4.0 is what >=0.3.3 resolves to for any build
# after 2026-09-07; vLLM 19f2c20e requires >=0.3.3.
FASTSAFETENSORS_SPEC=fastsafetensors==0.4.0
HUMMING_KERNELS_SPEC=humming-kernels[cu13]==0.1.12
XGRAMMAR_REF=v0.2.5
XGRAMMAR_COMMIT=2ea71da4ccb997a06928c9fb69b99f330da56697
XGRAMMAR_VERSION=0.2.5
XGRAMMAR_TRANSFORMERS5_COMPAT=1
VLLM_RUNTIME_EXTRA_PACKAGES=nvtx==0.2.15 nccl4py==0.4.1 nccl-extensions==0.1.0 cuda-core==1.0.1 cuda-pathfinder==1.6.0 cuda-tile==1.4.0 nvidia-cudnn-frontend==1.30.0

# ------------------------------------------------------------ patch toggles
# PATCH_IO_URING=on bakes liburing (the b12x loader's io_uring reader) and
# the seccomp profile; scripts/seccomp/spark-io-uring.json at 19f2c20e is
# byte-identical to f1c2508f (sha256 823b66051a52...): no daemon change.
PATCH_GPU_ARCH=auto
PATCH_HOST_ARCH=auto
PATCH_PCIE_ENV=auto
PATCH_PIPCHECK_WHEELTAG=auto
PATCH_VLLM_REQ_MARKERS=auto
PATCH_VLLM_WHEEL_TAGS=auto
PATCH_EXLLAMAV3_AVX=auto
PATCH_DEEPGEMM_LIBDW=on
PATCH_IO_URING=on
